Z||000000||MooCow||05-08-2001||03:53 PM||||Well still have yet to get my car back to normal.  I did replace the O2 sensor and it was nasty looking.  The only times that it smokes is when I go about 70MPH. Other than that no smoke.  It only comes out of the exhaust.  I have no other codes at all.  So I emailed Ed and asked what I could do.  He said:  "Doubt the 3.4 was bad (too low amount of miles) and it ran too good until<BR>you started to work on it!!!!!. <P>If you want to bring it down, and if only minor adjustments are needed,<BR>that will only cost you the $ for the trip. We won't charge for the shop<BR>time or for our couch."<BR>So do you think I should or see if someone around here can fix it?? Any other clues what it may be??  Trying to keep the Fiero faith alive but it is slowly dying.<P>                              Thanks Ken<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Alex4mula||05-08-2001||04:37 PM||||You said you bought the car from him. I don't know how far it is for you but if it was me I would go. Who better than him to check it out.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hartz||05-08-2001||04:39 PM||||GO!  You'll never know until you give it a try.  Assuming the car runs well enough to get you there and back, you're only out time and effort.  If you get it down there and they can fix it - you win.  If you get it down there and find out it's something major - well, at least you know.  If you get it down there and they're stumped too, well, at least you don't feel so bad.<P>Best of luck, let us know how it turns out.<P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo||||reg||14
